{"title":"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Solution_2_but_organized_w_table)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Solution 2 but organized w table)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>At Typico High School, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd7edd3842c40dbc1e54e522917a6e07b43c92e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of the students like dancing, and the rest dislike it. Of those who like dancing, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb7e03ccc8985ba9d029ea4add6e3e15ab9a953a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> say that they like it, and the rest say that they dislike it. Of those who dislike dancing, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/870303feff6f491471061a7402eba3e326ba84f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> say that they dislike it, and the rest say that they like it. What fraction of students who say they dislike dancing actually like it?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/c/d9cf7ef3caeb80bf4554aed5a7ac90b1ef6ed57b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 10\\%\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 12\\%\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 20\\%\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 25\\%\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 33\\frac{1}{3}\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"483\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/9/ad97a432193998cdfc0a95b74c4020b22bc0b5ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\% \\cdot 20\\% = 12\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"16\" /> of the people that claim that they dislike dancing actually like it, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/8/4b8209b610be49c76532d526f581a4c1d38c448a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40\\% \\cdot 90\\% = 36\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"14\" /> of the people that claim that they dislike dancing actually dislike it. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/3/fe3f2b9d074019cf706990b3050c7145dc07ca19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12\\%}{12\\%+36\\%} = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 25\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"198\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>~edits by flyingkinder123\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume WLOG that there are 100 people. Then 60 of them like dancing, 40 dislike dancing. Of the ones that like dancing, 48 say they like dancing and 12 say they dislike it. Of the ones who dislike dancing, 36 say they dislike dancing and 4 say they like it. We want the ratio of students like it but say they dislike it to the total amount of students that say they dislike it. This is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11e6dd5c955df6012fb7ad6d8b211f17d1619938.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{12+36}=\\frac{12}{48}=\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"148\" height=\"40\" />. We choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/8/1a83bbf71b192741ca183ddaee6f5850edee9601.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) } 25\\%}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"82\" height=\"31\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Solution_2_but_organized_w_table.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Solution_2_but_organized_w_table)\">Solution 3 (Solution 2 but organized w table)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Solution 2 but organized w table)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>WLOG, assume that there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> students at Typico High School. We make a chart: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00e0840c407a2b7befb90f0284eed20090036c84.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}[t]{|c|c|c|c|}\\hline &amp; \\text{Likes dancing} &amp; \\text{Doesn&#39;t like dancing} &amp; \\text{Total} \\\\\\hline \\text{Says they like dancing} &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\\\hline \\text{Says they don&#39;t like dancing} &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\\\hline \\text{Total} &amp; &amp; &amp; 100 \\\\\\hline \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"571\" height=\"83\" />\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of the students like dancing (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd7edd3842c40dbc1e54e522917a6e07b43c92e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />), so we fill that in: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/414807861c35918830138b892ce704b54c5a0f08.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}[t]{|c|c|c|c|}\\hline &amp; \\text{Likes dancing} &amp; \\text{Doesn&#39;t like dancing} &amp; \\text{Total} \\\\\\hline \\text{Says they like dancing} &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\\\hline \\text{Says they don&#39;t like dancing} &amp; &amp; &amp; \\\\\\hline \\text{Total} &amp; 60 &amp; &amp; 100 \\\\\\hline \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"571\" height=\"83\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/7/bb7e03ccc8985ba9d029ea4add6e3e15ab9a953a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$80\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of those <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kids say that they like dancing, so that's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/f/5afbad0b221f0ef70186fe70b08e6fc1efdd8dfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kids who like dancing and say that they like dancing. The other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> kids like dancing and say that they do not. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf590b7fec89806c347b0d94b4f22f127105caf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}[t]{|c|c|c|c|}\\hline &amp; \\text{Likes dancing} &amp; \\text{Doesn&#39;t like dancing} &amp; \\text{Total} \\\\\\hline \\text{Says they like dancing} &amp; 48 &amp; &amp; \\\\\\hline \\text{Says they don&#39;t like dancing} &amp; 12 &amp; &amp; \\\\\\hline \\text{Total} &amp; 60 &amp; &amp; 100 \\\\\\hline \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"571\" height=\"83\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students do not like dancing. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/870303feff6f491471061a7402eba3e326ba84f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$90\\%$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> of those <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/7/78792fe4680a164f537ea72a4f900e4471433c3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> students say that they do not like it, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of them. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/9/5f90e56b1010445c1c9f65d65e21bf2c4a3764e5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}[t]{|c|c|c|c|}\\hline &amp; \\text{Likes dancing} &amp; \\text{Doesn&#39;t like dancing} &amp; \\text{Total} \\\\\\hline \\text{Says they like dancing} &amp; 48 &amp; &amp; \\\\\\hline \\text{Says they don&#39;t like dancing} &amp; 12 &amp; 36 &amp; \\\\\\hline \\text{Total} &amp; 60 &amp; 40 &amp; 100 \\\\\\hline \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"571\" height=\"83\" />\n</p><p>At this point, one can see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/b/99b03e495a960f2f354a50e1ba9c4c715c1e108d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12+36=48$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> total students who say that they do not like dancing. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of those actually like it, so that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37eea0493273e341e5f1a816a84a8056f5975bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{12}{48}=\\dfrac14=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }25\\%}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"171\" height=\"38\" /> \n</p><p>For the sake of completeness, let us fill out the rest of the table. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/4/974f9dd034103c939ed723223424f741ae1f62d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{tabular}[t]{|c|c|c|c|}\\hline &amp; \\text{Likes dancing} &amp; \\text{Doesn&#39;t like dancing} &amp; \\text{Total} \\\\\\hline \\text{Says they like dancing} &amp; 48 &amp; 4 &amp; 52 \\\\\\hline \\text{Says they don&#39;t like dancing} &amp; 12 &amp; 36 &amp; 48 \\\\\\hline \\text{Total} &amp; 60 &amp; 40 &amp; 100 \\\\\\hline \\end{tabular}\\]\" width=\"571\" height=\"83\" />\n</p><p>~Technodoggo\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/93lThricxLE\">https://youtu.be/93lThricxLE</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5YbrPLGz5uM\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5YbrPLGz5uM</a>\n</p><p>~Math4All999\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B\">2017 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2017 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017234009\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.056 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 257/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2324/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7021/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.332      1 -total\n 60.18%    8.023      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 38.85%    5.179      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15427:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017234009 and revision id 291450. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}